+### Full-dataset qualification (2026-10-14)
+
+Eight local runs: Seed-TTS-Eval EN (1,088 items) and ZH (2,020 items),
+Omni/HF, B1/B4. Each run used one exclusively allocated, otherwise-idle H100
+80GB; backend/locale groups ran on separate GPUs. Both backends used the same
+native checkpoint and ordered datasets, BF16, seed 0, `max_tokens=2048`,
+CFG 1.3 and 10 diffusion steps. Omni used the deploy defaults (TP1/PP1).
+Each configuration warmed up with one same-size batch, then measured one
+full-dataset pass. Warmup consumes RNG state; matching seeds do not imply
+identical waveforms across backends or batch sizes.
+
+Generation wall time is the sum of batch timers, including prompt processing,
+generation, GPU completion and audio D2H. It excludes model startup, warmup,
+reference-file reads, WAV writes, shutdown and quality evaluation.
+Aggregate RTF = generation wall / generated audio duration, including all
+outputs regardless of ASR success or natural termination.
+
+Both outputs were evaluated after generation and engine release using
+`vllm_omni/benchmarks/data_modules/seed_tts_eval.py` in the same Omni evaluation
+environment: Whisper-large-v3 for EN, Paraformer-zh for ZH, and WavLM-base-plus
+embedding cosine for SIM. Intermediate WAVs used float32 storage before the
+shared 24 kHz mono PCM16 evaluation conversion. WER/SIM are per-item means;
+SIM is a proxy, not a perceptual-quality or speaker-verification guarantee.
+
+| Corpus | Backend | Batch | WER | SIM | Natural stop | Gen. wall (s) | Audio (s) | RTF |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| EN | Omni | 1 | 0.0501 | 0.8623 | 1088/1088 | 1589.7 | 5000.3 | 0.3179 |
+| EN | HF | 1 | 0.0599 | 0.8649 | 1088/1088 | 2248.5 | 4908.0 | 0.4581 |
+| EN | Omni | 4 | 0.0658 | 0.8625 | 1088/1088 | 614.1 | 5137.6 | 0.1195 |
+| EN | HF | 4 | 0.0563 | 0.8631 | 1088/1088 | 813.8 | 4996.5 | 0.1629 |
+| ZH | Omni | 1 | 0.0249 | 0.8742 | 2020/2020 | 4092.2 | 12814.4 | 0.3193 |
+| ZH | HF | 1 | 0.0269 | 0.8709 | 2019/2020 | 6100.5 | 13380.7 | 0.4559 |
+| ZH | Omni | 4 | 0.0277 | 0.8724 | 2020/2020 | 1479.9 | 13214.3 | 0.1120 |
+| ZH | HF | 4 | 0.0300 | 0.8726 | 2020/2020 | 2373.3 | 13177.9 | 0.1801 |
+
+- EN WER/SIM cover all 1,088 items in each run. Omni ZH B1 and B4 each have
+  one `empty_asr` result, so their means cover 2,019 items; HF ZH covers all
+  2,020. Empty ASR is an evaluation outcome, not evidence of a particular
+  generation or recognizer failure. Natural termination is counted separately.
+- Omni's RTF advantage over HF is 1.44x/1.43x at B1 (EN/ZH), and 1.36x/1.61x
+  at B4. These are HF/Omni RTF ratios, not identical-output latency speedups:
+  the generated durations differ. Omni B1/B4 RTF ratios are 2.66x/2.85x.
+- Omni WER is lower in three configurations, but EN B4 is higher by 0.0095
+  (0.95 percentage points). SIM is close across backends. This single pass
+  does not establish statistical equivalence or explain the EN B4 difference.
+- These are single-pass qualification results, not a repeated benchmark or
